When working with Java programs, handling text is very common. In this blog, I’ll explain what a String is, how it works, and commonly used String methods in a simple way. 🔹 What Is a String in Java? A String in Java is a sequence of characters. Example: String name = "Java";
Here, "Java" is a string literal. 🔹 Ways to Create a String
String s1 = "Hello";
Stored in String Constant Pool Memory efficient 2️⃣ Using new Keyword String s2 = new String("Hello");
Creates a new object in heap memory 🔹 Why Strings Are Immutable? In Java, String objects are immutable, meaning their values cannot be changed. Example: String s = "Java"; s = s.concat(" Programming");
A new object is created instead of modifying the existing one. 🔹 String Constant Pool The String Constant Pool (SCP) is a …

